
The object-configuration-based LOSO protocol holds out one of the 10 object
configurations as the external test fold while the room and sensor geometry
remain fixed. The held-out fold is not used for model fitting, preprocessing
statistics, scaling, early stopping, or parameter selection.

Random Forest uses 200 trees. Extra Trees uses 300 trees. The SGD-based linear
SVM uses hinge loss, L2 regularization, balanced class weights, a maximum of
5,000 iterations, and training-fold-only standardization.

Deep-learning early stopping uses an internal validation subset derived only
from the external training fold. The external LOSO test fold remains unused
until final evaluation.
